# Real to integer conversion of values exactly halfway between integers.
# Implementation-defined: ed.2 2.5.1.5.1 says the conversion rounds to
# the nearest integer and, for a tie, to the nearest even integer (IEC
# 60559 rule: 2.5 -> 2, 3.5 -> 4); ed.3 table 22 keeps "rounding to the
# nearest" and I do not have its tie rule at hand, so ties are recorded
# rather than required. Non-tie values are conformant in
# ops/real_conversions. The records are what IronPLC does: it truncates
# toward zero (3.5 -> 3, -3.5 -> -3), which is ironplc#1813 and also fails
# the non-tie cycles of ops/real_conversions; on ties alone a truncating
# and a round-half-to-even implementation agree on 2.5, -2.5 and 0.5 and
# differ on 3.5 and -3.5.
period_ms: 100
program: main
inputs: x l
outputs: i d
status: implementation-defined
reference: IEC 61131-3 ed.2 2.5.1.5.1 (round to nearest even), ed.3 table 22
---
0 x=2.5 l=2.5   => i=2 d=2
1 x=3.5 l=3.5   => i=3 d=3
2 x=-2.5 l=-2.5 => i=-2 d=-2
3 x=-3.5 l=-3.5 => i=-3 d=-3
4 x=0.5 l=0.5   => i=0 d=0
